    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Route support tickets to a small or large model by difficulty with Judgment\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Holds five support tickets in one field, then splits them into one item per ticket.\n2. Classifies each ticket in a single judgment call that answers three questions: the intent, whether it needs reasoning beyond routine procedure, and whether a short standard answer exists. Each question id carries the ticket id, so every answer says which ticket it belongs to.\n3. Sorts the answers by question, then zips the three lists into one item per ticket.\n4. Splits the tickets four ways: to a person when the classifier could not make sense of the ticket, to a canned answer when one exists, to a small model for routine work, and to a large model for the rest.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Install `n8n-nodes-judgment` from **Settings \u2192 Community Nodes**.\n- [ ] Add your **Judgment API** credential to the *Classify Tickets* node, and set the Base URL if you are not using the default provider.\n- [ ] Replace *Five Tickets* with your own source, keeping a `ticketId` and `ticket` field per entry. A helpdesk or webhook node fits here.\n- [ ] Attach a small chat model to *Small Model* and a larger one to *Large Model*, or replace both with your own handler.\n- [ ] Review the thresholds in *Route by Difficulty*: 0.6 for intent confidence, 0.5 for the other two.\n\n### Customization\n\nThe thresholds live in *Route by Difficulty*, not in the model, so re-tuning them re-routes the same tickets with no new inference. Tune the human branch first: raising the confidence gate sends more tickets to a person, which is the safe direction for anything customer-facing.",
        "width": 480,
        "height": 888
      },
      "name": "How This Works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -2032,
        16
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Install the community node first\n\n**Settings \u2192 Community Nodes \u2192 Install \u2192** `n8n-nodes-judgment`, then add your API key on the **Judgment API** credential. Self-hosted only: community nodes cannot run on n8n Cloud.",
        "width": 480,
        "height": 200,
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Install Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -2032,
        920
      ]
    }
